{"kind":"report","text":"CHANGES-REQUESTED on exact clean pushed head fad32567b74250be2efbfb05c0463789b4203cfd. Architecture: the affected layer is the semantic-free kernel store checkpoint cache. Compact v3, streamed reads, and the 256 MiB serialized ceiling remain unchanged, so this head does not require an architecture-page contract change. Security: the shared writer/decoder attachment ceiling and scratch release are sound, but the claimed construction-peak bound is false. writeEventReservingScratch admits new scratch using limit minus chunkBytes, tailBytes, and scratchBytes only; it omits the checkpointChunkWriter output capacity already retained and the equal growth-copy headroom its invariant reserves. Earlier no-scratch writes can grow output.Cap, then a scratch-heavy event can raise scratch while gzip emits no further underlying Write, leaving retained reserve plus scratch plus twice output.Cap above the limit with no check able to refuse it. TestCheckpointCacheBorrowedChunkBudgetsSortingScratch models twice output length rather than the production buffer capacity, so it does not witness this case. The focused tests pass but are non-probative for the defect. Simplification: keep one construction invariant by giving the scratch preflight the concrete chunk writer/output capacity; require reserve with the new scratch plus twice output.Cap to fit before allocation, hold scratch through the event write, and replace the synthetic length model with an exact/one-byte-short regression that first grows the production cap and then raises scratch on an event causing no later underlying gzip write. Supersede artifact d60858cd, repair, publish a new exact-head artifact, and request fresh review.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:d60858cd5f0fbf6dfc133832bed0a7ece205c23a","head":"fad32567b74250be2efbfb05c0463789b4203cfd","verdict":"changes-requested"}}